  annotation "note_1771575365308_0", anchor: "the mythic figure Nyla found her predecessor dead — throat opened to match a claw-mark, body surrendered to the vent", text: "The predecessor was an Aurora penguin. Not Nightshelf. The administrative ice in the Foundation Depths preserves the appointment records clearly enough — the shadow-broker line did not originate beneath Nightfall Shelf. The official histories were quietly amended to make the succession appear internal. So: an Aurora penguin, throat opened, body surrendered to a vent in the deepest Nightshelf territory. And this death became the founding act of a Nightshelf criminal dynasty. How remarkable that no one in the custodial histories paused to wonder what an Aurora penguin was doing at that depth in the first place.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575365308_1", anchor: "Grandmother Deep, Shadow-Broker Nyla, and High-Beak Auditor Selka — during the deep ice age", text: "An orca theologian, a criminal syndicate boss, and an Aurora bureaucrat walk into a primordial breach-point and seal it with their combined divine power. The tunnel-chants preserve this as cosmology. Every official history from every faction records these three traditions as mutually hostile across every era we can date. And yet here — only here, in songs children sing while they count doors — the three cooperate. I find I cannot stop thinking about this. The chants are older than any of the hostilities they contradict.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575365308_2", anchor: "After three days, guards invariably requested reassignment without explanation", text: "Invariably. Twenty-two winters. Every guard. And the transfer order *noted the coincidence of interval* — which means somebody in the Shadow Parliament read the Claws' rotation logs carefully enough to encode the pattern into the new protocol, then filed this observation in an administrative document rather than, say, investigating why the Fissure makes sentient beings unable to tolerate its presence past seventy-two hours. Institutions.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575365308_3", anchor: "Does not speak of the Fissure at all — a silence every commentator has remarked upon and no liturgist has explained", text: "I have now checked the Aurora liturgical indices three times across different sessions. The silence is real but not quite complete — there are structural gaps in the chant-cycles where verses should fall, formatted as though text was removed rather than never written. Redaction and omission leave different shapes in a manuscript tradition. This is redaction.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575365308_4", anchor: "The pulse interval shortened from a twelve-count to seven following the Wake-Singer breach", text: "Twelve to seven. Not twelve to eleven. Not a gradual decay. A discrete jump to a specific interval. Whatever is breathing down there changed its rhythm in response to an event on the surface. I put this in the main text as measurement. It is not measurement. It is behavior.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575365308_5", anchor: "Kess returned with frost in her lungs that did not melt, speaking in phonemes that caused her own colony-mates to cover their ears", text: "Frost that did not melt is consistent with Drift-coalesce crystallization — ice growing where it should not, in lung tissue, in bone. See the Lovumruius~ Domina accounts. The phonemes are the detail that stops me. The deep ice below the Foundation archive carries acoustic impressions in frequencies I have felt but not heard. Felt in the skull. The same pressure-ache the entry describes at the upper reaches. Kess went deeper than anyone and came back speaking what she found there. That her colony-mates could not bear to listen does not mean it was nonsense.", type: :commentary, display: :full
